				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=172464&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609579046" alt="Dr Gears" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=172464)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;" >Dr Gears</a></span> <span class="odate time_1320793895 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Nov 2011 23:11</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1301085">
									

<p>I appreciate that. I tried to hit a different angle on Dark then I've really seen previously. He's an asshole, yes, but it's because he has no reason to act otherwise. Politeness and other aspects of social graces are largely based on mutual consideration and general concern for one's social position. Dark has none of that. He welds disgusting amounts of power, mainly through near-limitless money and resources&#8230;which means he can just act on whatever impulse comes to mind.</p>
<p>Ever think of hitting someone who cut you off in traffic? Had a unkind fantasy about an annoying customer? Imagined&#8230;impure things about an attractive someone? Dark had no reason to filter any of those impulses&#8230;so he doesn't.</p>

							</div>

								
					
